---
const features = [
  {
    title: "One graph",
    body: "Reads Cargo.toml, package.json, pyproject.toml, Anchor.toml, and go.mod. kdo graph prints the edges. kdo affected --base main lists projects a change touches.",
  },
  {
    title: "A token cap",
    body: "kdo context <project> --budget 2048 returns the summary and public signatures that fit. Tree-sitter extracts signatures. File bodies stay on disk until a tool asks for one symbol.",
  },
  {
    title: "MCP, with a loop limit",
    body: "kdo serve --transport stdio. Tools: list, context, symbol, graph, affected, search, run. The same call 3 times (OpenClaw) or 5 times (other profiles) returns a loop error instead of another model turn.",
  },
  {
    title: "Specs in a worktree",
    body: "kdo apply -f spec.yaml, then kdo factory daemon. Plan, implement, and review use your key. The tester runs the test task from kdo.toml. Writes stay in .kdo/worktrees/<run>/. A pass merges only if git status is clean outside .kdo/.",
  },
];
---

<section class="relative mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-24 sm:px-6 sm:py-32">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl text-center">
    <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-tide">commands</p>
    <h2 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-5xl">
      Find the projects. Cap the context. Serve it.
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-5 text-lg text-ink-3">
      An agent that opens a monorepo by walking the tree reads files the task never needed. kdo already knows the projects and the dependency edges, and it will not return more context than the budget you set.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-16 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
    {
      features.map((f) => (
        <article class="glass relative overflow-hidden rounded-2xl p-6 transition-colors duration-150 ease-out hover:bg-white/70">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-medium tracking-tight text-ink">{f.title}</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-3">{f.body}</p>
        </article>
      ))
    }
  </div>
</section>
